WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.052
EXISTS asks only whether the inner query returns at
least one row The

00:00:06.079 --> 00:00:12.129
actual selected value inside the subquery usually
does not matter That

00:00:12.155 --> 00:00:17.726
is why SELECT one is common The business meaning is
simply does any

00:00:17.752 --> 00:00:23.682
related row satisfy this condition This makes EXISTS
especially natural

00:00:23.708 --> 00:00:25.063
for relationship checks
